From 447a3c4bb7a628688d3738a14dd833e8781aafb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:55:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 115/144] hydra, scene: subdivision creases, corners, boundary
 rules and holes

The subdivision tags were read from the prim's root, where Hydra does not
put them (they live in the mesh's container): every crease and corner was
lost. Read from the mesh schema now, with USD's sharpness (to 10) divided
by 10 for Cycles' weight (which it multiplies by 10 for OpenSubdiv);
corners are read without creases too; interpolateBoundary and
faceVaryingLinearInterpolation reach the mesh's boundary and face-varying
rules.

Holes on subdivided meshes: Cycles' mesh gets a per-face hole flag
(subd_hole); the dicing skips those faces while OpenSubdiv still shapes the
neighbours with them, as USD's holes mean.

Mesh::clear now also clears the vertex creases, which piled up on every
topology rebuild (K-72, tools/bench_subdiv.py: 7 cases against Karma).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/mesh.cpp | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 src/scene/mesh.cpp |  5 ++++
 src/scene/mesh.h   |  3 ++
 src/subd/split.cpp |  3 ++
 4 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

